      {
        "key": "li:7518612209258754048",
        "platform": "li",
        "label": "infographics-insights",
        "author_name": "Useful Infographics",
        "text": "More people should mean more speed.\n\nSo why does the opposite happen?\n\n\nGreat post by: Stephanie Hills, Ph.D.\n\n\nOriginal post below\n\n\n⬇️⬇️⬇️\n\n\nMore people should mean more speed.\n\nSo why does the opposite happen?\n\nJeff Bezos made the idea famous with Amazon’s “two-pizza team”:\nKeep teams small enough to move fast, communicate directly, and own the work.\n\nThere’s math behind that.\n\n2 people = 1 communication path\n5 people = 10\n10 people = 45\n\nAs the team grows, the number of possible communication paths grows much faster than the headcount.\n\nAt Scientific-Atlanta, Comcast was our largest customer, and we were doing joint software development.\n\nWe worked together to transform our development teams and organization to Agile software development.\n\nOne lesson became very clear with Agile:\nSmall, focused teams move differently.\n\nThey communicate faster.\nThey make decisions closer to the work.\nThey have clearer ownership.\n\nNow AI is making this idea relevant all over again.\n\nBecause we’re no longer only designing teams of people.\nWe’re designing teams of people + AI agents.\nAnd the question changes.\n\nIt’s not simply:\n“How many agents should we add?”\n\nIn an agentic system, one agent can orchestrate others.\nA supervisor agent can route work.\nSpecialist agents can own specific tasks.\n\nAgents can pass work without every agent needing to communicate with every other agent.\n\nSo the real design question is:\nHow do we add capability without adding unnecessary complexity?\n\nBecause more agents can still create more handoffs, more context transfers, more decision points, and more places for something to fail.\n\nGood orchestration changes the equation.\nWhether you’re designing an Agile team or an agentic system, the goal is not the biggest team.\n\nIt’s the clearest system that can get the work done.\n\nHuman or AI.\n\nWhat’s the smallest team you’ve seen do surprisingly big work?\n\n______________\n\n\nDM us to be featured on our next post\n\nFollow for more Useful Infographics",
        "created_at": "2026-10-21T10:00:39.747000+00:00",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/infographics-insights_more-people-should-mean-more-speed-so-why-activity-7518612209258754048-D8ir"
      },
